### Describe the bug

SWC seems to get confused when using type annotations within a ternary operation.

The type annotation in line 4 of the reproduction example causes swc to wrongly throw a syntax error.

### Input code

```typescript
function exampleFunction() {
  return Math.random() > 0.5
    ? `<button               
        @click="${(): void => console.log('this line causes a syntax error')}"
      ></button>`
    : `<button               
        @click="${(): void => console.log('this line does NOT causes a syntax error')}"
      ></button>`;
}
```


### Config

```json
{
  "jsc": {
    "parser": {
      "syntax": "typescript",
      "tsx": false
    },
    "target": "es2022"
  },
  "module": {
    "type": "es6"
  },
  "isModule": false
}
```


### Playground link

